$/={key_terms_data:[{term:"Deductible",meaning:"A fixed amount you must pay before the insurer pays any admissible claim. In indemnity plans, it is a rupee. [3]",effect:"The insurer starts paying paying only after deductible is crossed."},{term:"Co-payment",meaning:"A percentage of the admissible claim that you must bear. It does not reduce the sum insured, but reduces what insurer pays pays for that claim.",effect:"You share the bill in a fixed ratio, such as 0% or20%."},{term:"Waiting period",meaning:"A period after policy start during which certain claims are not payable. Standard policies generally have30-day initial waiting period, and pre-existing-disease waiting are commonly cappedat36months in newerIRDA-regulated-products[7]",effect:"Claims during the waiting period may be fully rejected."},{term:"Room-rent limit",meaning:"A cap on hospital room charge covered by the policy, often linked to a percentage of the sum insured.[2]",effect:"If you choose alier room, some policies reduce payment for other hospital charges in the same proportion."},{term:"Exclusions",meaning:"Treatments or situations the policy does not cover at all, such as pre-existing-existing disease during the waiting period, many non-medical items, cosmetic, care, and other listed exclusions.[132]",effect:"The insurer pays nothing for excluded items or events."}],examples_data:[{example:"1: Deductible and co-payment",scenario:"Assume policy has deductible of  Wakononononon"Room-rent plus exclusion:Assume a policy caps room rent at INR5000 per day but you choose room costing  Hungary a policy applies proportionate reduction insurer may reduce related hospital hospital charges charges in the same1:1: Hungary111111111111111111111110111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111